Z||000003||The Fieromaster||12-20-2001||11:40 AM||||I ran a 15.7 with an old tired 170,000 mile engine in my 85GT!!  AND i was practically sleeping off the line... I ran a 16.0 TORCHING my clutch the WHOLE track with my 85 fastback with modded motor... i KNOW i could do LOW 15-high 14s with her now!<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||12-20-2001||11:43 AM||||The fastest I've seen is 15.1 with manual trans, and 15.8 with automatic. The 1/4 mile times on stock engines can vary since some engine just run better than others. When they mass-produce engines, the HP can vary as much as 10% from the average. So some will be slower and some will be faster. I think it was Motor Trend who did an experiment with 10 Camaro's a few years back. They had 10 identical cars and tested them. 0-60 times varied by .75 seconds and 1/4 mile times varied by 1.5 seconds. I think out of the 10 cars 3 were faster than the "printed average", 2 were average and 5 were slower than average. If you use that as a rough estimate 30% of all cars are faster than advertised.||||reg||1
Z||000005||LoW_KeY||12-20-2001||06:08 PM||||15.1 with my car and a crappy clutch.. and 70,000 on the 2.8, but ever since the clutch was put in right it rips off the line like crazy! <P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/low_keysig.gif"> ||||reg||1
